    {
      "id": "37726058",
      "title": "Understanding the API Request",
      "sourceHash": "313f2f53ef4a8632931daf817911cba648cdf6464b0cf41ce19a7ff29b79e96e",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.1,
          "end": 4.29,
          "en": "When running our Python code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.29,
          "end": 8.7,
          "en": "we received this output down here in the terminal.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 8.7,
          "end": 12.54,
          "en": "This output is the API response we received,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 12.54,
          "end": 15.69,
          "en": "and as we learned in this module, to get a response,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 15.69,
          "end": 18.39,
          "en": "we have to send a request first.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 18.39,
          "end": 19.38,
          "en": "In this request,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 19.38,
          "end": 23.82,
          "en": "we have to define what type of information, what question,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 23.82,
          "end": 28.29,
          "en": "what prompt in the end we want to send to the API.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 28.29,
          "end": 31.77,
          "en": "Now, the whole management of this request, so to say,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 31.77,
          "end": 35.49,
          "en": "is defined inside our completion variable,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 35.49,
          "end": 38.643,
          "en": "specifically inside this \"create\" function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 39.51,
          "end": 43.8,
          "en": "This function contains different so-called parameters,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 43.8,
          "end": 46.44,
          "en": "like model and messages in here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 46.44,
          "end": 49.95,
          "en": "and these parameters configure the request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 49.95,
          "end": 52.08,
          "en": "So, one of the parameters we have to define",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 52.08,
          "end": 55.53,
          "en": "to send the request is the model parameter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 55.53,
          "end": 57.72,
          "en": "We talked about this on the slide already.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 57.72,
          "end": 62.31,
          "en": "In our case, we use the GPT 3.5 Turbo model.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 62.31,
          "end": 64.92,
          "en": "We could also use GPT Four instead,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 64.92,
          "end": 68.43,
          "en": "for example, or other models,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 68.43,
          "end": 71.28,
          "en": "but keep in mind that depending on the endpoint,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 71.28,
          "end": 74.49,
          "en": "chat completion, or completion, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 74.49,
          "end": 77.163,
          "en": "only specific models are supported.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 78,
          "end": 80.22,
          "en": "Besides the model parameter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 80.22,
          "end": 83.4,
          "en": "we also have this messages parameter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 83.4,
          "end": 86.37,
          "en": "Messages, so plural here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 86.37,
          "end": 89.19,
          "en": "We'll understand this in a few minutes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 89.19,
          "end": 90.023,
          "en": "For the moment,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 90.023,
          "end": 93.15,
          "en": "we can't just analyze the messages parameter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 93.15,
          "end": 97.97999999999999,
          "en": "which contains a so-called list, a Python list,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 97.97999999999999,
          "end": 102,
          "en": "and this list then contains a so-called dictionary.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 102,
          "end": 104.37,
          "en": "Now, we won't dive too deep into Python",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 104.37,
          "end": 106.74000000000001,
          "en": "and programming in this module,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 106.74000000000001,
          "end": 108.36,
          "en": "but the idea of such lists",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 108.36,
          "end": 111.24000000000001,
          "en": "and such dictionaries is to store information",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 111.24000000000001,
          "end": 113.643,
          "en": "which can then be accessed afterwards,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 114.47999999999999,
          "end": 117.09,
          "en": "and the list here allows us to store one,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 117.09,
          "end": 121.23,
          "en": "single in this case, or multiple dictionaries,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 121.23,
          "end": 124.23,
          "en": "so this part here in the Colibrasis",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 124.23,
          "end": 126.27,
          "en": "is one single dictionary,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 126.27,
          "end": 128.49,
          "en": "and the dictionary always contains",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 128.49,
          "end": 133.2,
          "en": "so-called key and value pairs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 133.2,
          "end": 137.31,
          "en": "So, the key here is roll and the value is user.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 137.31,
          "end": 140.67000000000002,
          "en": "For the second key value pair inside this dictionary,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 140.67000000000002,
          "end": 145.32,
          "en": "we have content, and content here is just \"hello.\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 145.32,
          "end": 148.92000000000002,
          "en": "Now, what this means in simple words is that we want",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 148.92000000000002,
          "end": 152.64,
          "en": "to send the following message to ChatGPT",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 152.64,
          "end": 154.563,
          "en": "when sending our request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 155.55,
          "end": 158.04,
          "en": "Our role is the role of the user,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 158.04,
          "end": 163.04,
          "en": "so we are the person that wants to interact with the API,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 163.26,
          "end": 166.17000000000002,
          "en": "and the content, the second key here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 166.17000000000002,
          "end": 170.82,
          "en": "we want to send to the API is simply \"hello.\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 170.82,
          "end": 172.14,
          "en": "If we would change this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 172.14,
          "end": 174.933,
          "en": "from hello to a question,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 176.79,
          "end": 181.79,
          "en": "like, for example, what is the capital of France?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 184.65,
          "end": 188.67,
          "en": "And now, rerun our Python file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 188.67,
          "end": 192.48,
          "en": "We get back, \"The capital of France is Paris.\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 192.48,
          "end": 195.24,
          "en": "So therefore, with the user role in here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 195.24,
          "end": 197.4,
          "en": "and the content key,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 197.4,
          "end": 202.323,
          "en": "we can define what the user wants to ask the API.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 203.34,
          "end": 205.2,
          "en": "Now, to make this a bit more interactive,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 205.2,
          "end": 208.5,
          "en": "instead of hard-coding the user input,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 208.5,
          "end": 211.29,
          "en": "we can just add a dedicated variable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 211.29,
          "end": 214.44,
          "en": "for this user input that allows the user",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 214.44,
          "end": 217.2,
          "en": "to directly ask the question or write",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 217.2,
          "end": 220.2,
          "en": "down the instruction in the terminal.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 220.2,
          "end": 223.86,
          "en": "For this, we'll just create a user input variable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 223.86,
          "end": 226.5,
          "en": "and set it equal to input.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 226.5,
          "end": 229.41,
          "en": "Input here is a Python function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 229.41,
          "end": 233.043,
          "en": "a predefined Python function, which could just say,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 235.117,
          "end": 239.97,
          "en": "\"Add your prompt in here.\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 239.97,
          "end": 242.13,
          "en": "Now, we add a space, and with this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 242.13,
          "end": 245.22,
          "en": "we can replace this hard-coded value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 245.22,
          "end": 248.553,
          "en": "for the content key with user input.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 249.51,
          "end": 254.51,
          "en": "By now, rerunning our code, we get \"Add your prompt,\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 255.81,
          "end": 259.5,
          "en": "and now, we could ask, what is Python, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 259.5,
          "end": 263.64300000000003,
          "en": "and by hitting enter, we get back the answer from the API.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 266.22,
          "end": 271.02,
          "en": "So, this is how we send our request in a very simple form.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 271.02,
          "end": 273.9,
          "en": "Before we have a closer look at the answer,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 273.9,
          "end": 276.06,
          "en": "at the response we get,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 276.06,
          "end": 279.27,
          "en": "I wanna explore a few more core parameters we",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 279.27,
          "end": 281.343,
          "en": "can add to our request.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ],
      "lectureOrder": 268,
      "videoOrder": 268
    },
    {
      "id": "37726062",
      "title": "Adding Parameters",
      "sourceHash": "98c434a0e1d58a681289c0e98fe4b8a56d47f37e5d3b278f519c243aacc32c65",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.6,
          "end": 2.94,
          "en": "So I'm back in the API reference,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 2.94,
          "end": 6.753,
          "en": "specifically in the create chat completion API reference.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.86,
          "end": 10.71,
          "en": "The parameters we can configure differ",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.71,
          "end": 15.27,
          "en": "depending on the selected endpoint you're using.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 15.27,
          "end": 19.41,
          "en": "I will focus onto the chat completion here for the moment.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 19.41,
          "end": 21.72,
          "en": "So in our request body,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 21.72,
          "end": 24.21,
          "en": "we can define the model parameter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 24.21,
          "end": 26.22,
          "en": "We had a look at this parameter already.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 26.22,
          "end": 28.967,
          "en": "We have this messages parameter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 28.967,
          "end": 32.37,
          "en": "with the role and content keys.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 32.37,
          "end": 35.73,
          "en": "We saw these already for the role of the user,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 35.73,
          "end": 39.45,
          "en": "and the content being the message sent by the user",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 39.45,
          "end": 41.31,
          "en": "to the API.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 41.31,
          "end": 44.19,
          "en": "These are, by the way, required parameters.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 44.19,
          "end": 46.98,
          "en": "So we always have to add these to our request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 46.98,
          "end": 48.57,
          "en": "Therefore, these are also part",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 48.57,
          "end": 51.03,
          "en": "of the example request obviously.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 51.03,
          "end": 53.43,
          "en": "Another quite interesting parameter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 53.43,
          "end": 56.1,
          "en": "is the so-called temperature though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 56.1,
          "end": 59.37,
          "en": "Temperature simply defines the randomness",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 59.37,
          "end": 63.45,
          "en": "of the output that is created by ChatGPT.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 63.45,
          "end": 67.23,
          "en": "You can have a temperature from zero up to two.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 67.23,
          "end": 68.52,
          "en": "The higher the value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 68.52,
          "end": 71.34,
          "en": "the more random the output will be.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 71.34,
          "end": 75.717,
          "en": "If we add this parameter to our request after our messages,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 78,
          "end": 82.47,
          "en": "so we simply add temperature right here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 82.47,
          "end": 85.77,
          "en": "and now you can define a value from zero up to two",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 85.77,
          "end": 86.76,
          "en": "as I said.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 86.76,
          "end": 89.82,
          "en": "If I use zero, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 89.82,
          "end": 94.82,
          "en": "and now rerun the code and again ask what is Python?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 97.02000000000001,
          "end": 99.093,
          "en": "And then I do this again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 101.00999999999999,
          "end": 104.1,
          "en": "Then if we compare our two answers,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 104.1,
          "end": 107.1,
          "en": "these are actually equal.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 107.1,
          "end": 108.9,
          "en": "But if it would now change the temperature",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 108.9,
          "end": 111.53999999999999,
          "en": "from the minimum value of zero to two,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 111.53999999999999,
          "end": 113.43,
          "en": "which is the maximum value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 113.43,
          "end": 118.143,
          "en": "and now rerun the app and again ask what is Python?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 120.51,
          "end": 123.84,
          "en": "Then the creation of the output takes a lot longer",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 123.84,
          "end": 126.36,
          "en": "and the output is actually also longer",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 126.36,
          "end": 130.77,
          "en": "and also distinguishes significantly from the output we had",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 130.77,
          "end": 134.883,
          "en": "for the two requests we sent with a temperature of zero.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 135.78,
          "end": 139.5,
          "en": "So I'll stick with a default value of round about 0.2",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 139.5,
          "end": 140.373,
          "en": "for the moment.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 141.6,
          "end": 144.32,
          "en": "The other core parameter you should ce aware of",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 144.32,
          "end": 147.273,
          "en": "is the max_tokens parameter down here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 148.14,
          "end": 150.03,
          "en": "Now, very important, we talked",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 150.03,
          "end": 153.9,
          "en": "about tokens already and we learned that different models",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 153.9,
          "end": 156.6,
          "en": "have a different maximum capacity",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 156.6,
          "end": 159.6,
          "en": "of tokens these can keep as context",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 159.6,
          "end": 162.127,
          "en": "for a specific chat, for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 162.127,
          "end": 165.21,
          "en": "The max_tokens here are different.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 165.21,
          "end": 169.65,
          "en": "These max_tokens just limit the length of the output.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 169.65,
          "end": 173.34300000000002,
          "en": "So of the response you get for your API request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 174.24,
          "end": 178.47,
          "en": "If we also add this parameter to our body here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 178.47,
          "end": 179.89,
          "en": "the so-called request body",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 180.9,
          "end": 185.9,
          "en": "and say we wanna have only 10 tokens, for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 186,
          "end": 191,
          "en": "Now again, run the code and ask what is a banana,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 191.76,
          "end": 194.193,
          "en": "which is a very creative question here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 196.44,
          "end": 200.1,
          "en": "Then I get back a banana is a long curved fruit with a,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 200.1,
          "end": 203.49,
          "en": "and that's it because you reached the maximum amount",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 203.49,
          "end": 205.35,
          "en": "of token that was defined",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 205.35,
          "end": 208.82999999999998,
          "en": "as part of the so-called request body.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 208.82999999999998,
          "end": 212.31,
          "en": "If I increase this to 100 tokens, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 212.31,
          "end": 215.013,
          "en": "then by asking the same question,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 218.34,
          "end": 222.45,
          "en": "we get hopefully back a full, a complete answer.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 222.45,
          "end": 223.923,
          "en": "And indeed, this worked.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 224.79,
          "end": 227.097,
          "en": "So these are the maximum tokens we can define",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 227.097,
          "end": 232.097,
          "en": "for the output, for the response for the API request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 232.44,
          "end": 235.32,
          "en": "And as mentioned, this limit is a different limit",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 235.32,
          "end": 239.16,
          "en": "than the model-specific token limit that differs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 239.16,
          "end": 240.903,
          "en": "from model to model.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 241.83,
          "end": 243,
          "en": "Now, you can dive deeper",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 243,
          "end": 246.84,
          "en": "into other parameters that are available depending",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 246.84,
          "end": 248.787,
          "en": "on the endpoint you are using.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 248.787,
          "end": 252.93,
          "en": "But with these core parameters, you're actually well set",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 252.93,
          "end": 255.96,
          "en": "and ready to work on your own APIs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 255.96,
          "end": 257.07,
          "en": "Before we do that though,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 257.07,
          "end": 261.18,
          "en": "we have to understand the response object in detail",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 261.18,
          "end": 264.693,
          "en": "and also dive deeper into our messages parameter.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ],
